  <div class="about-grid"><div class="about-copy panel"><span class="eyebrow">IDENTITY / STORY</span><h2>HOW I GOT HERE</h2><p>I’m Gabriel, a software engineer from Mexico. I started out with industrial systems and moved into mobile and web development. I've worked with Swift and iOS, backend integrations, and real-time monitoring. Every project has taught me something different.</p><p>When I'm not coding, I'm usually listening to metal, playing video games, or picking up my guitar to play some rock and heavy metal. I also like learning about networking and cybersecurity. I'm currently studying Norwegian and would love to become fluent one day.</p><p>Oh, and I’m a big fan of Cruz Azul and the Seattle Seahawks.</p><p>Music is a big part of my life. If you're into music too, <a class="inline-link" href="https://open.spotify.com/user/12137688570?si=60bcae74be154a7c" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">follow me on Spotify ↗</a>.</p></div><aside class="about-side"><div class="panel info-panel"><span class="eyebrow">CURRENT INTERESTS</span><div class="interest"><span>01</span> THREE.JS & GAME DEVELOPMENT</div><div class="interest"><span>02</span> NETWORKING & CYBERSECURITY</div><div class="interest"><span>03</span> LEARNING NORWEGIAN</div><div class="interest"><span>04</span> GUITAR / ROCK / METAL</div></div><div class="panel quote-panel"><span class="eyebrow">A REMINDER</span><blockquote>“Don’t let the theory stop you from reaching your goal.”</blockquote><p>I still think about this quote from David Bombal when I get stuck learning something.</p></div></aside></div>
